[OFL-1.1]  SIL Open Font License 1.1
=====================================================================

kernel/font_glyphs.c
third-party/terminus-font/

The glyph shapes are Terminus Font, copyright (C) 2020 Dimitar Toshkov
Zhekov, with Reserved Font Name "Terminus Font". The license text and the
authors file are in third-party/terminus-font/.

Why it is here. The glyphs were drawn for this project to begin with,
because the bitmap fonts shipped with a typical Linux system are GPL. Then
Russian, Ukrainian and Greek testers arrived, and fifty hand-drawn Cyrillic
letters turned out to look like fifty letters drawn one at a time: the
height wandered, the weight wandered, and words came out as a smear. Type
design is a craft. Terminus is a console font drawn by somebody who does it.

What OFL asks, and how each is met:

  the notice is kept            third-party/terminus-font/OFL.TXT ships with
                                the source and is named in the file header

  the font is acknowledged      this entry, and the header of
                                kernel/font_glyphs.c

  a Reserved Font Name is not   nothing here is called Terminus. The file is
  used for a modified version   kernel/font_glyphs.c and the data is a
                                converted subset - a modification - so the
                                reserved name stays behind.

  OFL material is not sold      it is not. It is bundled inside software,
  on its own                    which OFL permits explicitly.

OFL places no condition on the license of the software it is bundled into.
MIT here and OFL there is a combination OFL was written to allow.


[NOT DISTRIBUTED]
=====================================================================

build/
boot/efi/
